faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The Kath2 network is healthy. Thorough inspection of every component in the reported fault path found no anomaly. The Office LAN (192.168.3.0/24) is served by router1, which has UP interfaces on all four ports and a complete RIP routing table: Server Room routes (1.0.0.0/8) and Internet Lab routes (128.168.0.0/16) are learned from router2 via the 20.0.0.0/8 WAN link, and IT/CS subnets (192.168.1-2.0/24) are learned from router0 via the 10.0.0.0/8 WAN link. Router2 has the correct RIP configuration advertising all three of its directly connected networks and has full return routes to all campus subnets. Router0 is similarly healthy. All three RIP daemons are running, their update timers are current (last update < 30 seconds ago on all neighbours), and IP forwarding is enabled on every router. No iptables rules exist on router1 or router2. All office hosts carry the correct default gateway (192.168.3.1). Live ping tests from three different office devices (office_pc, enquiry, tpo) to the Server Room (pc1 at 1.0.0.5) and the Internet Lab (pc2 at 128.168.0.2, pc3 at 128.168.0.3) all returned 0% packet loss with normal latency. The ticket's claim that office PCs cannot reach the Server Room or Internet Lab does not reflect any observable fault in the network. The reported symptom is a false premise — there is no network anomaly to fix.
=== END ===